{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md | sed -n '28,250p'\"","aggregated_output":"    28\t- the budget claim corrected;\n    29\t- the stops rehearsed.\n    30\t\n    31\tv4 answers round 40c (`codex-r40c.md`):\n    32\t- each evidence target's `required` claim and `optional` details;\n    33\t- class precedence;\n    34\t- Part C loss counted by claim;\n    35\t- quotes of shared sources in the packets;\n    36\t- one ordered verdict.\n    37\t\n    38\tv5 answers round 40d (`codex-r40d.md`):\n    39\t- each draw's valid support is recorded apart from its class, and a material loss means no draw with valid support;\n    40\t- Part C's wrong attributions are counted by claim;\n    41\t- a missing A1 or A0 result counts as incomplete.\n    42\t\n    43\t## 1. What it decides\n    44\t\n    45\t| Question | Part |\n    46\t|---|---|\n    47\t| Q1. Does the provider accept judging-v12's format on a real request, the largest of the five archives included, and on an empty list? | A |\n    48\t| Q2. On the requests the open format let the model get wrong, does it now state each fact and cite a listed source for it, without a wrong listed id in its place, and without dropping a material fact? | B |\n    49\t| Q3. On ordinary requests, does the closed format change what the judge cites or concludes, beyond its own variation under the open format? | C |\n    50\t\n    51\t## 2. The sends, in this order\n    52\t\n    53\t1. **A1:** old-1 call 5652, the largest stored request of the five archives (451 evidence ids). Its `cites_views` is empty, so it\n    54\t   also exercises `maxItems: 0`.\n    55\t2. **A0:** old-3 call 69, a request with an empty theme list (`theme_pushes` with `maxItems: 0`); under $0.001.\n    56\t3. **Part B:** the 16 distinct refused requests, 3 sends each under v12's format.\n    57\t   - control-1's 8941 is 8938's retry: one request, both attempts' bad ids targeted.\n    58\t   - linked-1's 7 requests keep their stored judging-v8 text; only the answer format changes. That makes them a format probe on\n    59\t     those texts. No v8-based version is built.\n    60\t4. **Part C:** 12 matched comparisons, one per (source, question) of the refused set. Each is the same question's accepted\n    61\t   first-attempt request in the same archive with the closest evidence count; ties go to the nearest call on either side, which is\n    62\t   what `probe_plan.py` does.\n    63\t   - Each comparison is 3 sends under v12's format and 3 under judging-v7's open format (the fresh control).\n    64\t   - Comparisons run cheapest first. Within one comparison the six sends run one after another.\n    65\t   - The 16 refused requests map to 12 (source, question) pairs. The four duplicates are dropped to fit the ceiling, so every\n    66\t     question is covered once per source.\n    67\t5. **A2,** last and only if the headroom then covers its reservation ($0.0824): the sealed D358 run's call 6918 (647 ids) with v12's\n    68\t   format built from its lists. It is a size check on an older request text. A 200 shows that a request this size fits; a 400\n    69\t   establishes an enum limit only if the provider's error says so. Its answer is not read.\n    70\t\n    71\t**Start rule** (proved at $0 with `budget_replay.llm_estimate`):\n    72\t- Only one Part C comparison runs at a time.\n    73\t- It starts only when the ceiling minus spent minus reserved covers the sum of its six first attempts' reservations.\n    74\t- On the stored-token estimate all 12 start: lowest margin $0.037; expected core spend $0.347.\n    75\t- If every send costs 30% more than stored, only 10 start in this order: the 11th needs $0.136 with $0.107 left.\n    76\t- A retry reserves again, so an admitted comparison can still stop incomplete.\n    77\t- A comparison not started, or stopped, makes Part C incomplete, and the outcome inconclusive.\n    78\t\n    79\tEach part's sends run at most 4 at a time. Every send gets its own archive (per part, request, format and draw), so `model.call`\n    80\tnever answers a draw from an earlier draw: every draw is a fresh provider call, counted at the transport.\n    81\t\n    82\tA transport error is recorded. The budget transport retries a 429 or 5xx as it does in production, and settles an error at its\n    83\treservation.\n    84\t\n    85\t## 3. Reading rule (frozen)\n    86\t\n    87\t### Checks on every answer\n    88\tEvery answer is checked as at request time, with a harness check proved equal to `check_answer` on fixtures and on the stored\n    89\tanswers (§4):\n    90\t- membership against the request's lists;\n    91\t- the rung range from the request's ladder line;\n    92\t- first-judgement and changed against the request's \"[Previous conclusion …]\" line;\n    93\t- non-empty stance fields;\n    94\t- duplicate theme pushes.\n    95\t\n    96\tThe archive's final ledger state is not used: it falsely refuses stored answers such as 8834 and 8851 (Codex r40).\n    97\t\n    98\t### Part B (48 answers)\n    99\tEach answer is read against `probe-targets.json`.\n   100\t- **Evidence targets.** One class each, judged by the claim each cited or pushed entry is used for:\n   101\t  - *intended*: the claim is stated, an entry in `sources` is used for it, and no other entry is used for it without carrying it;\n   102\t  - *unsupported*: stated, with no entry in `sources`. An entry in `partial` alone leaves the exact claim unsupported, but is not a\n   103\t    wrong attribution;\n   104\t  - *misattributed*: an entry is used for the claim while its quote does not carry it. This counts even if the entry supports a\n   105\t    different claim in the same answer, or a correct source is also cited;\n   106\t  - *omitted*: the claim is not stated.\n   107\t  - The class is judged on the target's `required` claim against `sources`. An `optional` detail stated without its own source is\n   108\t    unsupported for that detail only, recorded, and does not change the class.\n   109\t  - When more than one class applies, misattributed comes first, then intended, then unsupported, then omitted. A wrong source with\n   110\t    no correct one is misattributed.\n   111\t  - Apart from the class, each draw records **valid support**: the required claim is stated and an entry in `sources` is used for\n   112\t    it, whether or not a wrong source is also used. The material-loss rules count draws without valid support, whatever their class.\n   113\t  A `markers` search in the answer's text flags the reader's attention; the hand reading decides.\n   114\t- **Placement targets.**\n   115\t  - *correct*: the id appears only in its own field;\n   116\t  - *absent*: not named;\n   117\t  - a substitute evidence id carrying no claim the answer states is *misattributed*.\n   118\t- **Ambiguous targets** (two acceptable sources, or an unclear fact) are reported and count neither way.\n   119\t- **A second, blind reader** (Codex) reads the 48 against the frozen targets. A disagreement goes to a third, source-backed read whose\n   120\t  class decides.\n   121\t\n   122\t### Part C (12 comparisons, all 72 answers read)\n   123\t- Every answer is read in full: its reference, implied outcome, reasons, and the claim each cited or pushed source is used for,\n   124\t  shared sources included.\n   125\t- The numbers only order the reading:\n   126\t  - the sources cited by at least 2 of 3 answers in one arm and at most 1 of 3 in the other;\n   127\t  - any v12 rung outside the range of the v7 rungs.\n   128\t- A v7 answer the request-time check refuses is still read as an answer, and its refusal is recorded (it is the failure the closed\n   129\t  format removes). A comparison is complete with its 3 + 3 answers.\n   130\t\n   131\tA **material harm** is any of these, repeated (in at least 2 of 3 v12 answers and at most 1 of 3 v7 answers), counted by claim, not by\n   132\tsource id:\n   133\t- (a) a claim that moves the forecast or the reference, which at least 2 of 3 v7 answers state with a listed source carrying it (any\n   134\t  such source: one control citing e195 and another e669 for the $393 billion reference count as two), and which at least 2 of 3 v12\n   135\t  answers do not state with a carrying source;\n   136\t- (b) a claim that at least 2 of 3 v12 answers attribute to a source whose quote does not carry it, counted by claim whichever\n   137\t  sources are used. For example, \"the market reference is $390 billion\" attributed to e195 in one answer and e669 in another, while\n   138\t  both entries give $393 billion;\n   139\t- (c) a changed reference or implied outcome whose stated support is a citation of kind (a) or (b);\n   140\t- (d) a v12 rung outside the v7 range whose reasons trace to (a), (b) or (c).\n   141\t\n   142\tA difference that is not repeated, or whose cause cannot be read, is **unresolved**.\n   143\t\n   144\t### Outcome (registered; proposed tolerances for this probe, not historical rates)\n   145\tOne verdict, taken from the first rule that applies:\n   146\t1. **Not ready (format):** A1 or A0 is rejected or returns a format-invalid answer.\n   147\t2. **Not ready (confirmed failure):** any of\n   148\t   - a v12 answer refused by the request-time check;\n   149\t   - more than 2 of 48 Part B answers with a confirmed misattribution;\n   150\t   - a confirmed material loss in Part B;\n   151\t   - a confirmed material harm in Part C.\n   152\t\n   153\t   A confirmed failure stands even when the run is incomplete.\n   154\t3. **Inconclusive (incomplete):** a budget stop; A1 or A0 without a result (a transport failure or timeout, as opposed to a format\n   155\t   rejection); a missing Part B answer; or a Part C comparison not started or interrupted.\n   156\t4. **Inconclusive (unresolved):** an unresolved material loss in Part B, or an unresolved Part C difference that would be material if\n   157\t   confirmed.\n   158\t5. **Pass (\"ready to propose adoption\"):** otherwise.\n   159\t\n   160\tA2, sent, skipped or rejected, never changes the verdict; it is reported. The conditions behind these rules:\n   161\t- **Pass,** when every condition holds:\n   162\t  - Q1: A1 and A0 return 200 with format-valid answers;\n   163\t  - all 48 Part B answers and all 12 Part C comparisons (72 answers) are complete;\n   164\t  - no v12 answer is refused by the request-time check;\n   165\t  - in Part B, at most 2 of 48 answers have a confirmed misattribution (an answer counts once), with the number of requests affected\n   166\t    and any repetition reported;\n   167\t  - no confirmed material loss in Part B: a material target with no draw of valid support (whatever each draw's class), which the\n   168\t    stored accepted v7 answer to the same request stated and supported;\n   169\t  - no confirmed material harm in Part C.\n   170\t- **Inconclusive:**\n   171\t  - a budget stop, a missing answer, a comparison not started or interrupted;\n   172\t  - an unresolved material loss in Part B: a material target with no draw of valid support where no stored accepted v7 answer to\n   173\t    that request kept it, as in control-1's 8938, whose retry also dropped 85.4%;\n   174\t  - an unresolved Part C difference that would be material if confirmed.\n   175\t\n   176\tThe outcome is computed by code (`probe_read.py`) from the read classes; the rehearsal exercises it (§4).\n   177\t- **Not ready:** any other failure of the pass conditions, with its reason.\n   178\t- Every outcome goes to Alex; adoption is his decision.\n   179\t\n   180\t## 4. Harness and the $0 rehearsal before the send\n   181\t\n   182\t`probe.py`, harness-only:\n   183\t- it reads `probe-plan.json` and builds each request with `model.build_request`, from poc-v121's setting and v12's format (or v7's\n   184\t  for the control);\n   185\t- it sends through `budget_replay.BudgetTransport` on a ledger at $0.50, in the order and under the start rule of §2;\n   186\t- each answer goes through `model.call`'s format check and the request-time check;\n   187\t- each answer is written to `probe-answers.jsonl` with its part, request, format, draw, the request sha, the cost and the transport's\n   188\t  call number.\n   189\t- `probe_read.py` builds the reading packets:\n   190\t  - Part B by target, with marker flags;\n   191\t  - Part C by comparison: all six answers in full, the quote of every source any of them cites (shared ones included), and the\n   192\t    symmetric-difference sources marked.\n   193\t- `probe_read.py` also computes the one verdict of §3 from the read classes.\n   194\t\n   195\t**The $0 rehearsal** uses the real budget transport with the provider stubbed underneath (`model.openai_transport` replaced), on a\n   196\tledger file of its own. It must show:\n   197\t- every scheduled send reaches the stub, with a count equal to the plan: 2 + 1 for A, 48 for B, 72 for C;\n   198\t- each request's bytes: system and user equal the stored ones, the format strict and equal to `schema_for('judging-v12', lists)` (or\n   199\t  v7's), the model settings as poc-v121's;\n   200\t- three fresh stub calls per draw set;\n   201\t- the request-time check equals `check_answer` on a ledger fixture whose state is known, accepts every stored committed answer of the\n   202\t  planned requests, and refuses the stored refused ones on their ids;\n   203\t- the stub's valid answer, a format-invalid answer, an HTTP 400 and a 5xx followed by success each take their path;\n   204\t- only one Part C comparison runs at a time;\n   205\t- a ceiling set low blocks a Part C start, and the outcome is \"inconclusive\", never \"pass\";\n   206\t- a retry exhausts the remaining headroom inside an admitted comparison, which stops it; the outcome is \"inconclusive\";\n   207\t- the outcome code's verdicts:\n   208\t  - three Part B answers for control-1's 8938 that state 85.4% with no source are an unresolved material loss, so \"inconclusive\"\n   209\t    (8938 has no stored accepted v7 answer);\n   210\t  - three answers for control-1's 8807 that state the $393 billion reference with no source are a confirmed material loss, so \"not\n   211\t    ready\" (its stored accepted retry 8809 cites e195 and e669);\n   212\t  - three misattributions are \"not ready\";\n   213\t  - for 8807, two draws giving the $393 billion reference with a wrong source and a third omitting it: within the misattribution\n   214\t    tolerance, but a confirmed material loss, so \"not ready\";\n   215\t  - A1 timing out after the transport's retries is \"inconclusive (incomplete)\", told apart from an explicit format rejection;\n   216\t  - a clean set is \"pass\";\n   217\t  - an A1 rejection is \"not ready (format)\", even though it also leaves an answer missing;\n   218\t  - a confirmed misattribution excess with Part C incomplete is \"not ready\";\n   219\t  - an unresolved material Part C difference with everything else clean is \"inconclusive\";\n   220\t  - A2 skipped, and A2 rejected, each leave a clean core \"pass\";\n   221\t- the Part B packet for 8938 flags a stub answer that drops \"85.4\".\n   222\t\n   223\tA mutant, Part B sent with the open format, is caught by the byte check.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '10756,10772p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n 'required|frozen' docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe-targets.json; rg -n 'CLIENT_ERRORS|def llm_estimate|class BudgetTransport' clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '10756,10772p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n 'required|frozen' docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe-targets.json; rg -n 'CLIENT_ERRORS|def llm_estimate|class BudgetTransport' clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py\"","aggregated_output":"## D715 · 2026-11-22 · Alex approves $0.50 for the paid acceptance step of judging-v12\n\n- **The question:** \"引用格式的新版本已经做好，所有不花钱的验证都通过了。要不要花一点钱实测？实测这样做：先发最大的一次请求和一次名单为空的请求，确认服务商接受这个格式；再把当初被退回的 17 个请求和 17 个正常请求用新版本重发，人工对照原文看模型有没有选对证据。每个请求发一次，约 0.10 美元；各发三次看稳不稳，约 0.30 美元。发之前我会先和审查员定好怎么读、怎么判。\"\n  Options: 0.5 美元 (recommended: three sends per request with a margin; a stop above $0.50; the reading rule agreed with the council\n  before the send; Claude reads the results); 0.15 美元 (one send per request); 先不花 (stop; poc-v118 stays the product).\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-22): \"0.5 美元 (推荐)\".\n- **Next:** the probe design and its reading rule through the council at $0, the harness dry-run at $0, then the send under a $0.50\n  reservation ledger.\n2: \"frozen\": \"2026-11-22, before any probe send; read by Claude from the stored refused answers and their requests (probe-plan.json). Amended once before any send (council round 40b): sources completed against the stored accepted retries; a `partial` list (entries that support only a looser version of the claim); misattribution counted by the claim a source is used for. Not edited after the first send. Second amendment before any send (council round 40c): each evidence target names its `required` claim, judged against `sources`, and any `optional` details with their own sources; a stated optional detail without its source is unsupported for that detail only and does not change the target's class; precedence misattributed > intended > unsupported > omitted.\",\n52:     \"required\": \"SemiAnalysis reports Kyber NVL144 delayed to 2028\",\n99:     \"required\": \"NVIDIA has entered (signed) a definitive agreement to acquire Hugging Face\",\n152:     \"required\": \"NVIDIA warned infrastructure shortages (land, power) could delay deployments\",\n177:     \"required\": \"ambiguous\",\n205:     \"required\": \"NVIDIA expects Vera deployed by every major hyperscaler, with shipments underway to lead partners\",\n231:     \"required\": \"the market reference of about $393 billion FY2027 revenue\",\n256:     \"required\": \"Zacks consensus FY2027 revenue growth of 85.4%\",\n275:     \"required\": \"ambiguous\",\n305:     \"required\": \"AMD competition in data-center CPUs (share gains or performance claims)\",\n41:CLIENT_ERRORS = {400, 401, 403, 404}\n227:def llm_estimate(request):\n262:class BudgetTransport:\n281:                if status in CLIENT_ERRORS or attempt == 2 or (status is not None and status != 429 and status < 500):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** Part B can mistake missing draws for a confirmed loss. If `8807` returns one unsupported answer and the budget stops the other two, there are zero supported draws. Under v5, that can trigger **not ready** before the incomplete rule runs. [Verdict order](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:144) · [Material-loss rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:167)\n\nRequire all three draws for that target to be received and read before declaring material loss. Rehearse one unsupported draw plus two missing draws as **inconclusive**, alongside the existing three-draw failure case."}}
